CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ from an lvalue: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ from a call: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ from a constructor argument: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [dcl.type.class.deduct]/1, [over.match.class.deduct]/5: class template
argument deduction uses the declaration's initializer whatever its form.
The front end deduced only from `(...)' and `{...}' initializers; `sp b = a;'
was "found no match for symbol 'sp'" (bin53).  libstdc++ 13's
_Sink::_M_write declares `span __to = _M_unused();', so its body was
dropped (format:2456) in every program using std::format.  g++ 13 and
clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
